{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall not swear by My name falsely</b> — why is this stated? Since it was already stated (Exodus 20:7), \"You shall not take the name of YHWH your Elohim in vain,\" one might think he is liable only for the special Name — from where do we include all the appellations? Scripture says, \"You shall not swear by My name falsely\" — every name that I have. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 19:12), from Torat Kohanim (parashah 2:6). And by way of truth, \"You shall not swear by My name\" is the special Name; \"and you shall not profane the name of your Elohim\" — this is Elohim, from which all the appellations proliferate. There too it states first \"the name of YHWH your Elohim\" and \"for YHWH will not acquit\" — by His great, special Name. And this is the reason for \"you shall profane,\" for when one swears by the special Name falsely, he profanes the name of his Elohim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:55:48.978249098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}